   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi <div><br></div><div>Just wanted to ask if anyone has had problems reading CWA files from axivity AX3 watches in different maximal g settings? </div><div><br></div><div>We have experimented with 2g 4g 8g 16g and the g.cwaread only seem to accurately read in 8g. Is there a way for the other g settings to be read into GGIR correctly or code changes to allow for higher or lower g settings?  <br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div><div>Kind regards </div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Ben Weedon</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">PhD Student</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">MSc Physiotherapy</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">BSc Sport Science</font></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt\">Sinclair Building SNC G.06</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt\">Centre for Movement, Occupational and Rehabilitation Sciences (MOReS),</span><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Movement Science Group, Faculty of Sport and Health Sciences<br>Oxford Brookes University</font></div><div style=\"font-size:12.