   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] Re: g.cwaread different g settings",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You are correct Ben. The g.cwaread function is probably not able yet to handle different dynamic range setting. I have only worked with 8g setting, so it has never been a priority for me.<div>This should be a matter of improving the code to extract and use the dynamic range from the file hear. That said, code contributions via pull requests or financial support to do these kind of improvements are always welcome.</div><div><br><div>Jairo&#39;s suggestion only affects the detection of signal clipping, but is not used in the process of reading the data.</div><div>Best, Vincent</div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
